Now let me also create a PoC for the `fu_coswid_firmware_parse_entity` vulnerability (stack buffer overflow in roles array). I need an entity with more than 6 role entries, each as a single uint:

CBOR structure:
```
Root map (2 entries):
  key: 0 (tag-id) -> value: "test" (text string)
  key: 2 (entity) -> value: map (2 entries)
    key: 31 (entity-name) -> value: "test" (text string)
    key: 33 (role) -> value: uint 1
    key: 33 (role) -> value: uint 1
    ... (7+ role entries)
```

Wait, CBOR maps can't have duplicate keys. Let me use an array of roles instead. Actually, looking at the code:

```c
} else if (tag_id == FU_COSWID_TAG_ROLE) {
        if (cbor_isa_uint(pairs[i].value)) {
                FuCoswidEntityRole role = cbor_get_uint8(pairs[i].value);
                entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] = role;
        } else if (cbor_isa_array(pairs[i].value)) {
                for (guint j = 0; j < cbor_array_size(pairs[i].value); j++) {
                        ...
                        if (entity_role_cnt >= G_N_ELEMENTS(entity->roles)) {
                                ...
                                return FALSE;
                        }
                        entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] = cbor_get_uint8(value);
                }
        }
```

The single uint case has no bounds check. But in a CBOR map, keys must be unique. So I can't have multiple `role` keys in the same map. However, I can use `fu_coswid_parse_one_or_many` which handles both single items and arrays. Let me check:

<｜｜DSML｜｜>
<parameter=command>cd /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/fwupd && grep -n "fu_coswid_parse_one_or_many" -A 20 libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-common.c</｜｜DSML｜｜>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

